From e854295302a6e35f93a7042eda3226e5af6fb72e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@advantech.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:06:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] imx8qxp_mek: adapt to Advantech ROM-5620 A1/A2

Minimal set of changes to run the i.MX8QXP MEK U-Boot on the
Advantech ROM-5620 A1/A2 module.

Device tree:
- rename the model to "NXP i.MX8QXP ROM-5620 A1/A2"
- run usdhc2 (SD) at 3.3 V only (no-1-8-v, no UHS modes) and ignore
  the write-protect line (disable-wp)
- move the mPCIe 3V3 enable to pca9557_a pin 0 and the USB OTG1 VBUS
  enable to GPIO4_IO03 (active low)
- add the virtual I2C mux binding to the i2cswitch@71 node
- drop the MEK-only board aliases, the MIPI-DSI/LVDS I2C buses and
  LDB1 nodes, and the FEC1 PHY reset GPIO
- mark pcieb as needed in SPL

Board code:
- power CAAM JR3 in SPL when CONFIG_DUAL_BOOTLOADER is set
- set up the RTL8211F PHY: LED configuration and RGMII TX/RX delays
- drive the external watchdog trigger (ADC_IN4 / GPIO1_IO14) high
- read the debug UART select pin (SAI0_RXD / GPIO0_IO27) and, when it
  is low, disable the kernel console and earlycon
- take the default kernel DTB name from CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE

Configuration:
- 8 DRAM banks, environment at offset 0x400000
- treat SD card detect as broken (CONFIG_MMC_BROKEN_CD)
- fastboot on USB controller 0
- enable the part command and random UUID support

Observation: ad hoc patch
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [other]

Signed-off-by: F. Aragon <francisco.aragon@advantech.de>
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@gmail.com>
